---
export const prerender = true;

import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="The Workshop · America's School Trust Library"
  description="What America's School Trust Library is building right now."
  sourceId="workshop"
>
  <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-a:text-blue-700 prose-a:underline">
    <p class="kicker">Work in progress</p>
    <h1>The Workshop</h1>

    <p>
      <span
        class="status-badge"
        data-library-status="workshop"
        aria-label="Library status: Work in progress. Workshop material; not verified."
        >Work in progress — nothing on this page is verified</span
      >
    </p>

    <h2>Now on the bench: the first verified claim set</h2>

    <p>
      The Library's first candidate for its Verified shelf is under
      construction: <strong>Canonical Claim Set 001 — Federal School-Grant
      Doctrine</strong>, a set of narrow propositions about the trust character,
      exclusive purpose, and full-value protection of the school-land grants,
      each tied to exact quoted language from six United States Supreme Court
      decisions spanning 1856 to 1989.
    </p>

    <p>
      Current state, plainly: thirteen claim records drafted; every quotation
      machine-checked against the retrieved opinions, twenty-nine of thirty
      passing verbatim; one quotation flagged for re-keying against the official
      reporter; two propositions held for narrowing; one held for counsel
      review.
    </p>

    <h2>The hornbook</h2>

    <p>
      The claim set is the first brick of a larger work: a one-volume reference
      on school-trust law, drafted in public with its verification flags
      showing. The
      <a href="/writing/books/school-trust-lands-hornbook/">working edition</a>
      is readable now, flags and all.
    </p>

    <h2>Also on the bench</h2>

    <p>
      The state files beyond Oregon, Utah, and Mississippi — thin today, growing
      by accession. The catalog's case-law gateways — 220 files held, 19 public
      so far.
    </p>

    <p>
      Want a bench of your own? The Library needs hands:
      <a href="/contribute/">how to help</a>.
    </p>
  </article>

  <style>
    .kicker {
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      font-size: 0.72rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.1em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: #A88A4E;
      margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
    }
    .status-badge {
      display: inline-block;
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      font-size: 0.66rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.075em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      padding: 0.2rem 0.6rem;
      border: 1.5px dashed #C9A24A;
      border-radius: 3px;
      background: #FBF3DF;
      color: #8a5f10;
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
